Following a detailed review of your current pension arrangement, I recommend switching to a new scheme that better aligns with your financial objectives and long-term retirement planning. This switch is in your best interests for the following reasons:

-  Lower Costs - The receiving scheme has a lower overall cost structure compared to your existing pension, meaning more of your savings remain invested for growth rather than being lost to charges. The plan itself is 0.06% more expensive than the recommended solution
-  Lifestyling - Your funds are currently invested in lifestyling funds, which automatically reduce investment risk as you approach retirement. As a result, your portfolio will eventually move outside of your agreed risk range. We would not recommend remaining invested in these types of funds.
